  "id": "fetch-surveil-land-keep",
  "name": "Fetch a surveil land at their end step, lands stay on top",
  "intent": "At the opponent's end step with fewer than five lands out, crack a fetch for a surveil land, Shadowy Backstreet first, then Meticulous Archive, then Undercity Sewers, and keep the surveilled card on top: the five-mana Overlord of the Balemurk and Quantum Riddler still need lands, a fetchland included. From five lands fetch-surveil-land bins lands instead. Only at 6 life or more and while fewer than two surveil lands are out. Stands down against eldrazi-ramp only: that matchup is at the per-archetype active-play cap, and against a ramp deck a surveil land entering tapped at their end step is worth less than leaving ephemerate-protect-lone-creature armed. Every other matchup is unchanged.",
